  "summary": "Seven preprints extend unconventional magnetism to quasicrystals, optical octupole probes, and nonlinear spin responses, alongside magnon-based transport proposals.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is symmetry-driven responses of unconventional magnets whose spin-space symmetry or order parameter departs from conventional ferromagnets and antiferromagnets. Altermagnetism is extended to moiré quasicrystals with high-order spin polarization, while octupolar magneto-optical effects offer field-free optical probes in altermagnets and noncoplanar antiferromagnets. Nonlinear spin generation and spin photocurrent are proposed as probes of spin-space symmetry, domains and quantum geometry. A related set addresses magnon physics: competing single-magnon and magnon-pair Berry-curvature contributions reversing the thermal Hall sign, gate-controlled nonreciprocal magnons in BiFeO3, and a large pseudo-orbital magnon moment in CrI3 nanotubes. A cavity proposal ties photon condensation to scalar spin chirality. All items are preprints and theoretical or proposal-level.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
